  "chapter": {
    "number": 40,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(41) For the end, a Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Blessed is the man who thinks, on the poor and needy: the Lord shall deliver him in an evil day.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "May the Lord preserve him and keep him alive, and bless him on the earth, and not deliver him into the hands of his enemy.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "May the Lord help him upon the bed of his pain; you have made all his bed in his sickness.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I said, O Lord, have mercy upon me; heal my soul; for I have sinned against you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Mine enemies have spoken evil against me, saying, When shall he die, and his name perish?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And if he came to see me, his heart spoke vainly; he gathered iniquity to himself; he went forth and spoke in like manner.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "All my enemies whispered against me; against me they devised my hurt.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They denounced a wicked word against me, saying, Now that he lies, shall he not rise up again?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For even the man of my peace, in whom I trusted, who ate my bread, lifted up his heel against me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But you, O Lord, have compassion upon me, and raise me up, and I shall requite them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "By this I know that you have delighted in me, because my enemy shall not rejoice over me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But you did help me because of my innocence, and have established me before you for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Blessed be the Lord God of Israel from everlasting, and to everlasting. So be it, so be it.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": []
  },
